WEBVTT

NOTE Scene 05. Speaker labels and dialogue derive from the original script.
NOTE Time positions aligned using faster-whisper word timestamps; human review still required.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
<v Jack Marlowe>Three days later, Victor Sterling's little empire was crumbling.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.280
<v Jack Marlowe>The authorities had the ledger and witness statements.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:12.020
<v Jack Marlowe>Ernest Cross had contacted his attorney, returned home, and was reportedly sleeping

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:12.760
<v Jack Marlowe>on the sofa.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.860
<v Betty>Hey, boss! Look at this! We're in the newspaper!

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.900
<v Jack Marlowe>What does it say?

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.940
<v Betty>Local detective helps expose millionaire fraud.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.840
<v Betty>Not a word about the secretary.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.100
<v Jack Marlowe>They have a limited amount of ink, Betty.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.860
<v Betty>Yeah? Well, I got a limited amount of patience.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.740
<v Vivian Cross>Good afternoon, detective.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.240
<v Vivian Cross>Betty.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.780
<v Betty>Hey, Mrs. Cross! How's married life?

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.380
<v Vivian Cross>Ernest is discovering the importance of communication.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.320
<v Jack Marlowe>I'm glad he's safe.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.780
<v Vivian Cross>So am I. The remainder of your fee, and a little something extra for your very

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.820
<v Vivian Cross>capable secretary.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.120
<v Betty>I knew I liked you, lady!

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.080
<v Jack Marlowe>Don't encourage her.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.500
<v Vivian Cross>I've arranged a lovely vacation for Ernest.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.200
<v Jack Marlowe>That's thoughtful.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.320
<v Vivian Cross>Three weeks. Somewhere very cold. He can practice his communication skills with

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:06.960
<v Vivian Cross>the penguins.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.720
<v Betty>Ain't love grand?

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.540
<v Vivian Cross>You've been absolutely wonderful, detective. Perhaps we'll meet again.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.680
<v Jack Marlowe>Preferably under less expensive circumstances.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.180
<v Vivian Cross>Goodbye, darling.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.240
<v Betty>Well, boss. Ya found a missing husband, exposed a crook, and got us enough

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.940
<v Betty>money to pay the rent!

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.080
<v Jack Marlowe>All in a day's work.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.860
<v Betty>Three days, actually. And I did most of it.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.120
<v Jack Marlowe>Let's not ruin a perfectly good moment with arithmetic.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:40.908
<v Betty>Marlow Detective Agency! How can I help ya?

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:44.140
<v Betty>Uh-huh. Your parrot? He's bein' blackmailed?

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.460
<v Betty>By who? Another parrot?

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.120
<v Betty>Boss! We got another one!

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.060
<v Jack Marlowe>I reached for my hat. In this city, trouble never slept.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.020
<v Jack Marlowe>And apparently, neither did the birds. But for now, the missing man was home,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.880
<v Jack Marlowe>the crook was caught, and the rent was paid.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.860
<v Jack Marlowe>Case closed.

